# The public web deploy is the marketing site plus the playground, which now
# includes the command centre itself: index.html and app.js ship byte-identical
# to what a running instance serves, answered by demo-api.js from a fixture.
# No instance is exposed by that — there is no server on this host at all, and
# demo-api.js is inert anywhere else. Everything still absent below is absent
# on purpose.
#
# NOTE: Vercel's Root Directory is the repo root, so this file — sitting
# inside the Output Directory it serves — is never actually read by Vercel as
# ignore rules; the real one lives at the repo root and only excludes secrets
# and build clutter, since Output Directory already scopes serving to this
# folder's contents regardless. This file survives as the tested manifest of
# what's meant to be public: the list below is exactly what test/demo.test.js
# and test/seo.test.js check was deliberately shipped.
